{% endif %}

This turn's narration:
<narrative>
{{ narrative }}
</narrative>
{% if request %}

What the player wants to see:
<request>
{{ request }}
</request>
{% endif %}

Requirements:
- Pick the most visual moment of this turn; if the player said what they want to see, draw that.
- Write one English paragraph of 60 to 150 words: who is in the picture, how each of them looks and is dressed, what they are doing, their expressions and poses; the place, time of day, light and weather; how close the camera is and the composition.
- The "I" of the narration is the protagonist. When the protagonist is in the picture, describe them from the description above; never write "I" or "me".
- Only describe what can be seen: no dialogue, thoughts or sounds, and no text in the picture.
- Don't name an art style; the style is added separately.
- In people, list who appears in the picture, spelling each name exactly as in the list above; leave out anyone not on the list.

Output only one JSON object in the form {"prompt": "English description", "people": ["Name"]}, with no other text.
